From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libc: inherited exec uses the active guest environment

AOSP exec.cpp argument collection adapted for the shared path execution layer.
The inherited forms must read the guest environ slot: glibc execvp otherwise
ignores guest clearenv/putenv (Termux JNI) and launches with the host environment.
Explicit envp is never filtered. PATH comes from the parent guest, as bionic
execvpe specifies. Variadic forms and fexecve route through mapped execve rather
than glibc internal calls. Services retain host PATH behavior.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -119,3 +119,4 @@
 		'libc/libc-environment.cpp', # apklayer: isolated app environment
+		'libc/libc-exec.cpp', # apklayer: inherited guest environment and PATH
 		'libc/libc-musl.c',
 		'libc/libc-signal.c',
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libc/libc-exec.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,109 @@
